                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Xonix-style games are really interesting to me, and this is the best version of that formula I've come across so far. Playing on a cube instead of a flat surface adds some surprisingly interesting depth in partial information and in how you move from one part of the map to another. Most of the \"stage hazards\", if you will, are well-trodden ground in the genre, but there's some unique ones and the implementation of adapted ones is very solid and feels more fair than a lot of implementations. There are a few rough edges - controls are odd, probably owing to this being adapted from controller, and the line scoring mode feels like more luck than skill - but this is still definitely worth picking up if you're interested in these kinds of games.",
